WEBVTT

00:13.840 --> 00:16.340
Nice to meet you all! We are-

00:17.260 --> 00:18.890
Diamond Dust.

00:19.640 --> 00:21.730
We're releasing our debut single-

00:23.180 --> 00:26.100
Time's ticking. This place isn't free, you know.

00:26.560 --> 00:28.770
I still think we should try finding a bassist.

00:29.770 --> 00:31.070
Would be nice if we could.

00:31.230 --> 00:34.780
But I think we're doing pretty well
with just the three of us for now.

00:38.160 --> 00:38.740
What is it?

00:38.910 --> 00:41.200
Who was that girl talking just now?

00:41.370 --> 00:44.160
No clue. Probably their new vocalist.

00:44.330 --> 00:45.710
Never saw her before.

00:45.870 --> 00:47.630
Did something about her catch your eye?

00:48.750 --> 00:49.840
<i>...It can't be, right?</i>

00:50.670 --> 00:52.510
Nevermind, it was nothing.

02:27.180 --> 02:31.480
RAISE YOUR VOICE

02:27.770 --> 02:28.980
Yo.

02:29.350 --> 02:32.110
If it isn't Momo-chan! How many years has it been?

02:32.560 --> 02:34.570
Come on, less than two probably.

02:35.860 --> 02:38.240
I see this place hasn't changed much.

02:38.990 --> 02:42.870
Sure it has, we're a hair away from going under here!

02:43.030 --> 02:44.450
You're our only hope.

02:46.040 --> 02:46.950
Is that you?

02:47.290 --> 02:49.290
No way, you were so cute!

02:50.120 --> 02:51.420
Oh shut it.

02:52.670 --> 02:54.630
<i>They just look alike...right?</i>

02:55.170 --> 02:55.800
Nina.

02:55.960 --> 02:56.880
Uh, yes?

02:57.210 --> 02:59.420
You can take a look inside if you want.

03:00.720 --> 03:02.640
We're coming in.

03:10.600 --> 03:14.900
It's much smaller than the stage we played on.

03:15.730 --> 03:17.780
We're supposed to fit in here, huh?

03:17.940 --> 03:20.400
Most live houses are about this size.

03:20.740 --> 03:23.410
Though this one's been around for a while,

03:23.570 --> 03:25.580
so it has its regulars.

03:25.910 --> 03:28.040
And they won't go easy on us.

03:28.700 --> 03:31.370
The boss said he'd like us to give it a shot.

03:31.540 --> 03:32.170
What do you think?

03:33.170 --> 03:34.130
A concert?

03:34.710 --> 03:37.170
Don't push yourself if you're not feeling up to it.

03:37.630 --> 03:40.050
We should probably practice some mo-

03:39.000 --> 03:40.050
I'll do it.

03:40.800 --> 03:42.180
At least hesitate a little.

03:42.340 --> 03:46.550
She's totally hooked now...you'd never think
she was freaking out so much last time.

03:47.010 --> 03:50.390
Well, we're talking about a 20-minute performance here.

03:51.430 --> 03:53.270
So it shouldn't be that big a deal.

03:54.270 --> 03:55.400
Let's try it.

03:56.730 --> 03:58.190
And here are your tickets.

03:58.780 --> 04:02.240
By the way, you're not allowed to advertise me
as a former Diamond Dust member, got it?

04:03.150 --> 04:06.410
I'm in a new band with these two, and-

04:11.580 --> 04:12.120
Here.

04:12.710 --> 04:14.580
No turning back now.

04:14.920 --> 04:15.750
What?

04:16.750 --> 04:18.590
THE NEXT DAY

04:19.130 --> 04:22.590
I didn't think we'd have to sell those ourselves...

04:24.180 --> 04:24.880
DID YOU SELL ANY?

04:26.010 --> 04:27.510
THERE'S NO WAY I DID

04:27.850 --> 04:29.810
I ONLY HAVE TWO LEFT

04:29.970 --> 04:30.770
NO WAY!?

04:30.930 --> 04:33.060
TRY YOUR PREP SCHOOL, THERE'S GOTTA BE SOMEONE THERE

04:33.310 --> 04:35.600
IT'S NOT YOUR HOMETOWN, SO IT'S NOT LIKE ANYONE WILL RECOGNIZE YOU

04:49.240 --> 04:49.990
What do you want?

04:50.290 --> 04:53.040
Well, uh, I'm doing a concert with my band...

04:53.250 --> 04:54.750
You...interested?

04:55.620 --> 04:56.500
You're in a band?

04:57.080 --> 04:57.790
Yes.

04:58.080 --> 05:00.090
I'm more into heavy metal...

05:00.250 --> 05:03.090
That's totally cool, we're uhhh...
sort of something like that.

05:06.260 --> 05:08.260
And you just gave it to her for free?

05:08.850 --> 05:10.510
Customers over profits!

05:10.680 --> 05:13.270
It's not like we're doing this for money.

05:13.520 --> 05:16.390
The point is to get lots of
people to come, isn't it?

05:16.560 --> 05:17.440
They won't come.

05:18.230 --> 05:20.190
Here's a life lesson for you.

05:20.360 --> 05:23.230
People hate it when something they paid for goes to waste.

05:23.400 --> 05:26.650
But if it was something they got
for free, they won't care.

05:27.660 --> 05:31.450
Also, giving out tickets for free
means we're the ones paying for them.

05:32.410 --> 05:35.710
-You really don't know anything, huh?
-Know what?

05:36.000 --> 05:39.420
Technically, we're the ones
buying those tickets.

05:39.580 --> 05:41.670
We paid the live house for them.

05:43.340 --> 05:45.090
Here you go.

05:45.590 --> 05:48.010
The minimum amount of tickets you need
to sell is lower these days,

05:48.180 --> 05:51.300
but in general, if you want to perform,
you need to pay performing fees

05:51.470 --> 05:54.600
and for a minimum amount of tickets.
That way even if no one comes to your concert,

05:55.060 --> 05:59.850
the live house is guaranteed at least the bare minimum profit.

06:00.150 --> 06:01.860
That's not fair!

06:02.190 --> 06:03.860
That's how the business works!

06:05.780 --> 06:06.990
Oh really...

06:10.530 --> 06:11.120
Huh?

06:15.330 --> 06:15.830
Here.

06:16.370 --> 06:18.040
Sorry for bothering you during your break.

06:18.750 --> 06:19.500
What do you want?

06:20.500 --> 06:25.010
I wish Momoka-san told us she was
paying for those tickets...

06:25.550 --> 06:28.880
Well, we're basically kids to her.

06:29.050 --> 06:29.630
How come?

06:29.930 --> 06:34.260
We're younger, and we're not exactly
functioning members of society yet.

06:36.310 --> 06:36.930
Hmm?

06:37.680 --> 06:39.520
Hey, Momo-chan's friends!

06:39.690 --> 06:40.810
Hi there!

06:44.610 --> 06:45.530
Is this a new thing?

06:46.650 --> 06:48.530
Uhh, where was it again...

06:48.820 --> 06:51.200
Is he trying to sell us tickets again?

06:51.360 --> 06:52.320
I don't think so.

06:52.490 --> 06:53.280
Oh, there they are.

06:53.740 --> 06:55.290
Here you go.

06:55.830 --> 06:56.750
What are these?

06:57.750 --> 07:00.670
Diamond Dust, that band that's getting their big break now,

07:00.830 --> 07:05.800
they used to play here a lot.
So they paid a visit earlier and left these.

07:06.130 --> 07:07.460
And you're giving them to us?

07:07.630 --> 07:09.800
They have this big agency backing them now,

07:10.220 --> 07:13.180
So I kind of lost interest.

07:14.600 --> 07:18.930
Do you know why Momoka-san left Diamond Dust?

07:19.350 --> 07:20.390
She didn't tell you?

07:20.690 --> 07:21.190
No.

07:21.600 --> 07:23.400
I don't know the details myself,

07:23.610 --> 07:26.480
but apparently the agency started making
a lot of changes to the band.

07:26.610 --> 07:28.480
Their look, songs and all that.

07:29.570 --> 07:32.160
She hated the idea and left.

07:33.110 --> 07:35.620
I have a ticket for her too if you want.

07:36.280 --> 07:38.500
So, are you gonna give it to her?

07:39.450 --> 07:43.210
No. I feel like we'll get into a fight if I do.

07:43.210 --> 07:45.920
But I...I want to see them for myself.

07:47.170 --> 07:49.170
Wanna go together then?

07:49.710 --> 07:51.630
I'm kinda curious myself.

07:52.760 --> 07:54.050
Subaru-chan...

07:56.260 --> 07:58.100
THE NEXT DAY

08:04.980 --> 08:07.520
You're the girl that gave me
concert tickets before, right?

08:07.940 --> 08:08.650
Yes.

08:08.900 --> 08:13.070
Do you still have some left?
Three of my friends want to come.

08:14.200 --> 08:16.200
That'll be 7500 yen in total.

08:16.660 --> 08:17.990
Eh, you were charging for them?

08:18.700 --> 08:21.160
You don't have to buy if you don't want to.

08:22.160 --> 08:24.540
You can't just flip it on her like that.

08:24.790 --> 08:26.290
Well what was I supposed to do?

08:26.630 --> 08:31.300
Something like "We were told to give them away at first so I did,

08:31.460 --> 08:34.090
but then the live house suddenly changed their mind!

08:34.260 --> 08:36.180
But since you're already a valuable customer,
I'll cut you a deal -

08:36.340 --> 08:38.560
Three for 2500 each instead of 3000 each. Sound good?"

08:38.810 --> 08:40.430
- That's called lying.
- That's called working hard.

08:41.270 --> 08:45.190
<i>Numbers 500 to 550, please enter the venue.</i>

08:48.860 --> 08:49.610
What is it?

09:00.240 --> 09:02.080
A full house, huh.

09:21.100 --> 09:27.440
<i>Stationary at a crossroads
that doesn't appear on any map</i>

09:27.600 --> 09:34.990
<i>What can I rely on
to find my way?</i>

09:50.040 --> 09:51.590
<i>It's your own fault, you know.</i>

09:58.840 --> 09:59.640
No way.

10:00.890 --> 10:01.640
It can't be.

10:01.810 --> 10:04.890
<i>Everything is so white
Everything is so slow</i>

10:05.060 --> 10:10.150
<i>All the answers are
void of substance</i>

10:11.060 --> 10:12.690
Don't you <i>dare</i> sing that song.

10:14.860 --> 10:16.280
Wait!

10:17.150 --> 10:20.660
I said wait! It's barely been 5 minutes
since the concert started, what's gotten into-

10:20.820 --> 10:22.580
- Subaru-chan.
- What?

10:22.740 --> 10:26.580
I'm this close to saying some
<i>really</i> nasty things right now.

10:26.750 --> 10:27.790
Just give me a sec.

10:28.420 --> 10:31.790
I need to let everything out.

10:34.720 --> 10:38.890
<i>*indistinguishable gremlin noises*</i>

10:39.050 --> 10:39.850
Damn it,

10:39.950 --> 10:41.140
JUST DIE!

10:41.390 --> 10:43.600
I think I understood that last part.

10:44.060 --> 10:47.450
What is this, what is this, WHAT IS GOING ON??

10:47.630 --> 10:48.440
Don't ask me.

10:48.980 --> 10:51.100
And it just had to be Diamond Dust.

10:51.310 --> 10:55.940
The one thing that's as precious to me as my life. My treasure.

10:56.480 --> 10:57.820
Are you going to explain what's going on?

11:01.070 --> 11:02.780
Their new singer.

11:03.370 --> 11:05.160
I know her.

11:06.240 --> 11:09.500
We used to be friends, but not anymore.

11:10.460 --> 11:11.620
Not anymore!

11:15.000 --> 11:16.380
<i>Girls Band Cry.</i>

11:19.880 --> 11:22.390
<i>Nice to meet you all! We are-</i>

11:23.350 --> 11:24.760
<i>Diamond Dust!</i>

11:27.810 --> 11:29.300
It's gonna break, you know.

11:29.420 --> 11:30.910
I don't want to listen to that.

11:31.060 --> 11:34.150
You barge into their concert, get pissed,

11:34.310 --> 11:35.900
and now you're acting like this.

11:36.070 --> 11:37.980
Do you know what they call people like that?

11:38.610 --> 11:40.200
Toxic fans.

11:40.400 --> 11:42.610
You can't possibly understand how I'm feeling right now.

11:43.030 --> 11:44.370
Good, because I don't want to.

11:44.700 --> 11:47.990
How is this even possible?

11:48.160 --> 11:51.000
How did that girl even become Diamond Dust's vocalist?!

11:51.160 --> 11:53.580
That shallow little-

11:53.750 --> 11:58.250
Well, if she's there, it means she
stood out enough to pass the auditions.

11:58.360 --> 11:59.160
So what if she-

11:59.260 --> 12:00.760
Oh shut it already.

12:01.090 --> 12:02.760
This is your problem, not theirs.

12:03.050 --> 12:06.510
Maybe it is, but I love and listen to Diamond Dust

12:06.680 --> 12:10.140
more than anyone else in that audience!

12:10.390 --> 12:12.270
This is exactly what makes you a toxic fan.

12:12.640 --> 12:15.060
Diamond Dust doesn't exist just for you.

12:15.230 --> 12:18.150
Then what about you,
are you really okay with this?

12:18.360 --> 12:19.730
Why wouldn't I be?

12:19.900 --> 12:22.280
They seem to be more popular than when I was there.

12:22.610 --> 12:24.030
So you're fine as long as they're popular?

12:24.200 --> 12:25.780
It's better than them not being popular.

12:26.070 --> 12:27.660
That's not what I'm asking!

12:30.620 --> 12:33.540
You're always sticking your nose
into other people's business.

12:33.790 --> 12:37.340
Like I said before, wasting time here
means wasting money.

12:37.500 --> 12:38.290
Subaru.

12:38.630 --> 12:39.630
This is pointless.

12:40.920 --> 12:43.720
We can't practice with you two like this.

12:43.930 --> 12:46.300
If you have steam to blow off,
better do it sooner than later.

12:49.600 --> 12:51.180
IZAKAYA

12:52.560 --> 12:54.690
- Well?
- Hold on a sec.

12:56.060 --> 12:57.690
That was not necessary.

12:58.110 --> 13:01.190
Also, who comes to a bar
in their school uniform?

13:01.690 --> 13:05.450
It's not like I'm drinking alcohol.

13:05.610 --> 13:08.780
Why are you always in your uniform anyway?

13:08.950 --> 13:11.160
Saves me the pain of choosing outfits.

13:11.330 --> 13:15.540
Also, high school girls get a lot of perks.

13:16.420 --> 13:17.250
Liar.

13:17.420 --> 13:19.840
Anyway, enough about me, have at it you two.

13:21.920 --> 13:23.210
Why are you always sticking up for them?

13:23.550 --> 13:25.340
I'm not sticking up for them or anything.

13:25.630 --> 13:28.180
Yes you are. Think about it,

13:28.350 --> 13:32.890
the current Diamond Dust has nothing
to do with the Diamond Dust you were in.

13:33.060 --> 13:33.730
So?

13:33.980 --> 13:36.480
Then why are you defending them? It makes no sense.

13:36.640 --> 13:38.150
I don't get the problem here.

13:38.310 --> 13:41.190
I'm not involved with them anymore. They can do whatever they want.

13:41.360 --> 13:44.740
Whatever path they choose,
I don't have the right to complain.

13:45.110 --> 13:47.280
I'm not asking for the right answer.

13:47.450 --> 13:49.320
I want to know how you actually feel about this.

13:49.990 --> 13:50.870
Whatever.

13:51.530 --> 13:52.990
I don't really care.

13:54.620 --> 13:56.410
But it was <i>your band.</i>

13:57.290 --> 14:00.000
The band you put your soul into.

14:01.460 --> 14:02.960
Don't just make your own assumptions about me.

14:03.670 --> 14:05.380
Fine, then I was wrong.

14:05.630 --> 14:07.740
I guess Diamond Dust was

14:07.890 --> 14:10.640
completely meaningless to you.

14:10.800 --> 14:11.890
Oh, give me a break.

14:12.390 --> 14:14.770
It's the new singer that's actually bothering you, isn't it?

14:14.930 --> 14:15.890
That's not it!

14:16.270 --> 14:19.900
I'm asking if you're really okay with the new Diamond Dust!

14:22.690 --> 14:24.940
Sorry everyone, please don't pay us any mind.

14:25.490 --> 14:27.110
Guys, turn down the volume a bit.

14:27.740 --> 14:28.610
Listen,

14:29.070 --> 14:33.280
Bands grow and change, just like people.

14:33.490 --> 14:35.620
It's an inevitable process.

14:36.080 --> 14:38.160
Then why did you leave?

14:39.870 --> 14:42.880
You left because you didn't like
that change you're talking about.

14:43.040 --> 14:46.970
Because they were becoming something
different from the Diamond Dust you knew.

14:48.090 --> 14:51.180
Because you were sure you weren't in the wrong.

14:51.340 --> 14:54.970
Because you hate what they're doing now!

14:56.390 --> 14:57.770
Why aren't you saying anything?

14:57.930 --> 15:00.150
Was the song I always listened to meaningless?

15:00.480 --> 15:02.520
I always thought that song was the heart and soul of DD.

15:03.020 --> 15:05.400
Just admit they changed!

15:05.820 --> 15:08.400
That whatever <i>that</i> was
isn't the real Diamond Dust anymore!

15:09.150 --> 15:09.990
That they're-

15:11.570 --> 15:12.660
Ugh...

15:14.830 --> 15:15.580
Shut up.

15:16.580 --> 15:17.410
I won't.

15:18.290 --> 15:22.290
I loved your Diamond Dust
more than anything.

15:30.680 --> 15:34.100
<i>Everything is so white
Everything is so slow</i>

15:34.260 --> 15:35.470
<i>All the answers</i>

15:35.640 --> 15:40.140
I loved your Diamond Dust
more than anything.

15:40.480 --> 15:43.100
That song changed my life.

15:44.400 --> 15:46.320
You can't just abandon it like that!

15:50.990 --> 15:54.700
You hate it, and you still tell yourself that
you're in the wrong and they're not.

15:54.990 --> 15:57.200
I don't want you to lie to yourself.

15:59.580 --> 16:03.290
Do you know what the original
Diamond Dust's dream was?

16:04.580 --> 16:05.630
What was it?

16:05.880 --> 16:10.550
To stay as a band together, with the
original members, until we were all wrinkled.

16:11.550 --> 16:13.090
To never quit no matter what.

16:13.590 --> 16:17.060
That was it. None of us cared about music style
or anything like that at first.

16:18.260 --> 16:20.680
That's why it's my fault.

16:24.060 --> 16:25.190
"Grit your teeth for now."

16:25.650 --> 16:29.530
"Once we make it big, we'll be
able to play the way we want to."

16:30.650 --> 16:34.110
They did everything they
could to make me stay.

16:35.990 --> 16:38.990
But it didn't work. I left them behind.

16:43.620 --> 16:45.250
Here you go. Oolong tea.

16:45.920 --> 16:47.250
Thank you very much.

16:48.380 --> 16:49.170
Nina.

16:49.550 --> 16:52.970
Sorry for the commotion everyone!

16:57.010 --> 16:57.890
Even so...

16:58.220 --> 17:01.520
I'm still a fan of yours.

17:02.310 --> 17:04.060
Because I love your music.

17:05.350 --> 17:09.820
Because the original Diamond Dust is the
only thing that touched my heart back then.

17:10.820 --> 17:12.110
And you were the heart of it.

17:17.950 --> 17:19.030
Idiot.

17:19.580 --> 17:20.910
You're making a mess of yourself.

17:21.870 --> 17:23.000
I know I'm an idiot.

17:23.330 --> 17:27.460
I wouldn't be here if I wasn't one.

17:29.630 --> 17:31.960
Keep the drinks coming!

17:32.170 --> 17:33.760
Subaru-chan...

17:34.630 --> 17:36.890
Huh? Hey, wai-

17:41.810 --> 17:45.100
Sorry, your face pissed me off.

17:46.270 --> 17:49.940
Momoka-san, I thought you could hold your liquor...

17:50.190 --> 17:52.280
Well, she did go at it pretty hard today.

17:52.440 --> 17:53.690
She reeks of alcohol...

17:55.860 --> 17:57.320
Hold up, you're dragging her!

17:57.490 --> 17:59.410
- Subaru-chan, grab the legs!
- Yessir!

18:04.450 --> 18:05.080
Like this?

18:05.250 --> 18:07.080
I don't think that's gonna work...

18:07.540 --> 18:10.340
Momoka-san? We're going to
put you down for a second...

18:11.460 --> 18:12.340
I'm sorry.

18:18.300 --> 18:19.010
I'm sorry.

18:21.260 --> 18:22.760
Maybe she was happy, you know.

18:23.470 --> 18:24.390
No...

18:26.390 --> 18:27.310
I don't think that's it.

18:37.360 --> 18:39.780
You should be the one to
choose our stage outfits.

18:41.030 --> 18:43.370
Having a friend you had a falling out with

18:43.540 --> 18:48.500
become the singer of your favorite group
isn't exactly a common experience.

18:49.000 --> 18:51.420
You should make something out of it.

18:51.580 --> 18:52.670
How?

18:53.960 --> 18:57.630
Letting your anger, joy,
and sadness run free,

18:57.920 --> 18:59.380
that's the great thing about being in a band.

18:59.550 --> 19:00.300
What's this?

19:00.800 --> 19:02.720
The poster for our concert.

19:03.640 --> 19:07.270
"Featuring Momoka, former member of Diamond Dust"?

19:07.520 --> 19:09.390
He's got some nerve!

19:09.890 --> 19:14.400
But you know, a good chunk of the people
that went to DD's debut live

19:14.570 --> 19:16.150
will definitely come thanks to this.

19:16.940 --> 19:20.610
Try to think about what kind of
impact you'd want to make on them.

19:22.280 --> 19:22.950
You're right.

19:24.450 --> 19:25.490
Outfits, huh...

19:26.750 --> 19:29.210
It's not like we have much money to spend...

19:30.830 --> 19:32.630
It's been three years already.

19:32.960 --> 19:36.550
Yeah, we were thinking
we'll have to make a big impact

19:36.710 --> 19:39.200
at the next competition.

19:45.760 --> 19:47.390
Ah, Momo-chan!

19:47.560 --> 19:48.480
Yo.

19:48.930 --> 19:50.480
Sorry!

19:50.730 --> 19:55.230
I told them not to write your name, but I guess
the staff couldn't pass up the opportunity.

19:55.400 --> 19:58.070
But you see, we got a full house thanks to that.

19:58.780 --> 19:59.650
Huh, what?

20:04.200 --> 20:05.780
So, do we have our outfits?

20:06.410 --> 20:09.040
Yes. I was thinking these would be good.

20:11.250 --> 20:11.920
Here.

20:12.080 --> 20:13.960
Did you make them together?

20:14.130 --> 20:15.840
We're open to criticism.

20:16.380 --> 20:18.250
Though you'll still have to wear them.

20:18.420 --> 20:20.510
Let's bare it all together.

20:22.470 --> 20:23.430
I see.

20:24.510 --> 20:25.600
I like it.

20:27.510 --> 20:28.770
You're supposed to be Momoka?

20:29.470 --> 20:30.430
Yeah, what of it?

20:30.770 --> 20:34.690
Sorry, but girly music's not my thing.

20:34.900 --> 20:36.440
Mind if I shake the atmosphere up a bit before you're up?

20:37.020 --> 20:38.610
We don't really care...

20:38.780 --> 20:41.900
Don't worry about us, we'll shake it ourselves.

20:44.820 --> 20:45.490
If you say so.

20:48.080 --> 20:48.910
Nice one.

20:56.920 --> 20:58.040
Momo-san!

20:58.210 --> 20:59.300
Momoka!

21:01.380 --> 21:03.840
Momoka! We love you!

21:08.510 --> 21:09.890
Wanna start?

21:10.810 --> 21:13.560
Impact...it's a nice word, don't you think?

21:14.440 --> 21:16.810
We struggle, we exhaust ourselves...

21:17.270 --> 21:21.400
we want to stick it to someone, even
at the cost of getting hurt ourselves.

21:22.530 --> 21:23.360
Yeah.

21:24.280 --> 21:27.820
You know, your song...
it pierced through my heart.

21:28.370 --> 21:29.910
It had an impact on me.

21:30.200 --> 21:32.290
It's as if it was telling me,
"Don't give up, even if you die trying".

21:35.500 --> 21:37.750
Let's make that impact!

21:41.590 --> 21:43.090
Scream out everything you're feeling.

21:43.260 --> 21:45.510
Leave nothing out.

21:45.680 --> 21:48.760
Let out all your frustrations, your shame,
yout anger, your sadness,

21:48.930 --> 21:50.850
your pathetic self, that past you hate
so much you want to

21:51.010 --> 21:53.640
crawl into a bed and die, and all those regrets that haunt you.

21:53.810 --> 21:55.480
Lay them all bare!

21:56.350 --> 21:59.360
Here we go!

21:59.860 --> 22:00.860
LIAR

22:01.440 --> 22:02.360
COWARD

22:02.690 --> 22:05.860
This is everything I've got!

22:04.530 --> 22:05.860
DROPOUT

22:13.870 --> 22:16.750
<i>What we found
at this tumultuous crossroads</i>

22:17.040 --> 22:20.000
<i>Hollow words
that end up crumbling</i>

22:20.170 --> 22:23.050
<i>A shooting star could
sweep everything away</i>

22:23.210 --> 22:26.260
<i>And yet, nothing seems to change</i>

22:26.420 --> 22:29.300
<i>We lie
to keep our hands clean</i>

22:29.470 --> 22:32.180
<i>Our dreams falling apart in the distance</i>

22:32.350 --> 22:35.270
<i>We pretend nothing
we hear nothing</i>

22:35.430 --> 22:37.890
<i>Watch the storm pass by</i>

22:38.810 --> 22:41.690
<i>The city is caught
in a whirlwind of truth</i>

22:41.860 --> 22:45.150
<i>Where should we
let ourselves be carried?</i>

22:45.320 --> 22:47.820
<i>If we can smile at the end</i>

22:47.990 --> 22:50.370
<i>May our hands be tied</i>

22:50.530 --> 22:51.410
<i>It's reality</i>

22:51.570 --> 22:54.370
<i>But we will only understand
once our dreams are abandoned</i>

22:54.540 --> 22:57.660
<i>Our wishes are never heard</i>

22:57.830 --> 23:00.380
<i>In a distorted world</i>

23:00.540 --> 23:04.840
<i>What can we do?</i>

23:08.590 --> 23:10.640
<i>What can we improve?</i>

23:14.720 --> 23:16.930
<i>Will you finally be discovered?</i>

23:20.980 --> 23:23.820
<i>Before everything collapses</i>

23:28.030 --> 23:29.900
<i>Let's shape in the shadows</i>

23:34.450 --> 23:38.620
<i>The vision that drives us</i>
